Cg a64.125000,65.000000,387
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
}
{\plain {Suppose we consider a "detection"
 problem- finding an object in an image.
 We shall consider a "one-dimensional image"
 for simplicity. We want to filter noisy
 image and find and estimate the position
 of an object. The data is "stored"- and
 so there is no reason to impose a causality
 restraint. It is convenient to have the
 processed signal, if present, be in its
 "true location". }}
}
.TXT 14 0 111 0
Cg a63.750000,65.000000,246
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
}
{\plain {We shall make the object very simple,
 of extent very small compared to M. We 
assume that the scene is "sensed" with a
 signal which "matched" to the FIR filter
 we have been discussing. The "block diagram"
 of the sensing system is shown below.}}
}
.EQN 9 -4 133 0
